  "figure": {
    "caption": "Shortcut bridging by the Markov chain of [AndresArroyo2018Bridging]: particles join two fixed sites (black squares) along the land (shaded); the nodes under the land are over the gap (red outline). One particle at a time (outlined) expands into a free neighbouring node and contracts forward with a probability that rewards a short perimeter ($\\lambda$) and penalises perimeter over the gap ($\\gamma$), otherwise it contracts back; moves that would disconnect the particles from the sites, or create a hole, are refused. Shown is a run of accepted moves: the bridge shortcuts the corner but keeps few particles over the gap.",
